# Roadmap Agent

---

# Overview

The Roadmap Agent is the final planning agent in the AI Software Architect Agent system. It is responsible for transforming the outputs generated by all previous AI agents into a structured software development roadmap.

Unlike traditional project planning, which requires manual effort from project managers and software architects, the Roadmap Agent automatically creates a complete project timeline, milestones, sprint plans, task priorities, resource allocation, dependency mapping, and deployment strategy.

The Roadmap Agent ensures that developers have a clear implementation plan before writing any code.

---

# Purpose

The primary purpose of the Roadmap Agent is to automate project planning by generating a step-by-step development roadmap based on the project requirements, architecture, database design, APIs, and documentation.

The generated roadmap helps developers estimate project duration, organize development tasks, and monitor project progress.

---

# Objectives

The Roadmap Agent aims to:

- Generate a complete software development roadmap.
- Divide the project into implementation phases.
- Create sprint plans.
- Estimate project duration.
- Identify project milestones.
- Define task dependencies.
- Recommend development priorities.
- Suggest testing phases.
- Generate deployment schedules.
- Support Agile software development practices.

